§§ `Conduct and determinations`

GIVEN `notice sent on`                 IS A MAYBE DATE
      `car moved without consent`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `recourse not preserved`         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The conduct after the loss`
`conduct with notice` `notice sent on` `, moved:` `car moved without consent` `, recourse lost:` `recourse not preserved` MEANS
    `The conduct after the loss` WITH
        `rescue or limitation measures not fully taken`                      IS FALSE
        `scene not protected, without an authority's direction`              IS FALSE
        `police not notified immediately`                                    IS FALSE
        `Tasco not notified immediately or its instructions not followed`    IS FALSE
        `written notice of the loss sent on`                                 IS `notice sent on`
        `force majeure prevented the written notice`                         IS FALSE
        `objective obstacle prevented the written notice`                    IS FALSE
        `Tasco assessed the damage within the notice period`                 IS FALSE
        `driver drowsy or asleep at the wheel`                               IS FALSE
        `vehicle moved, dismantled or repaired without Tasco's consent, when not necessary` IS `car moved without consent`
        `driver left the scene or did not follow alcohol or drug testing instructions`      IS FALSE
        `incomplete or untruthful declaration, or an increase in risk not notified`         IS FALSE
        `right of recourse not preserved or transferred, or a settlement made with the third party` IS `recourse not preserved`
        `information given dishonestly, concealed or falsified`              IS FALSE

-- Notice sent the day after the loss of 15 June 2025: no ground of Article 14 is met.
GIVETH A `The conduct after the loss`
`good conduct` MEANS `conduct with notice` (JUST (YMD 2025 6 16)) `, moved:` FALSE `, recourse lost:` FALSE

-- An objective obstacle kept the owner from writing; no notice sent within 5 days.
GIVETH A `The conduct after the loss`
`conduct with an objective obstacle and no notice` MEANS
    `The conduct after the loss` WITH
        `rescue or limitation measures not fully taken`                      IS FALSE
        `scene not protected, without an authority's direction`              IS FALSE
        `police not notified immediately`                                    IS FALSE
        `Tasco not notified immediately or its instructions not followed`    IS FALSE
        `written notice of the loss sent on`                                 IS NOTHING
        `force majeure prevented the written notice`                         IS FALSE
        `objective obstacle prevented the written notice`                    IS TRUE
        `Tasco assessed the damage within the notice period`                 IS FALSE
        `driver drowsy or asleep at the wheel`                               IS FALSE
        `vehicle moved, dismantled or repaired without Tasco's consent, when not necessary` IS FALSE
        `driver left the scene or did not follow alcohol or drug testing instructions`      IS FALSE
        `incomplete or untruthful declaration, or an increase in risk not notified`         IS FALSE
        `right of recourse not preserved or transferred, or a settlement made with the third party` IS FALSE
        `information given dishonestly, concealed or falsified`              IS FALSE

GIVEN `band 20 to 50` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `band 50 to 100` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `fault`          IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `Tasco's determinations`
`Tasco decided` `band 20 to 50` `,` `band 50 to 100` `, fault` `fault` MEANS
    `Tasco's determinations` WITH
        `rate chosen in the 20 to 50 per cent band`  IS `band 20 to 50`
        `rate chosen in the 50 to 100 per cent band` IS `band 50 to 100`
        `salvage value of a vehicle the owner keeps` IS NOTHING
        `fault ratio of the owner or driver`         IS `fault`

GIVETH A `Tasco's determinations`
`nothing decided` MEANS `Tasco decided` NOTHING `,` NOTHING `, fault` NOTHING

§§ `Own-damage losses`

GIVEN `the kind`    IS A `A kind of damaged item`
      `the cost`    IS A NUMBER
      `replaced`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`an item` `the kind` `costing` `the cost` `, replaced:` `replaced` MEANS
    `A damaged item` WITH
        `kind`                                                     IS `the kind`
        `cost`                                                     IS `the cost`
        `replaced`                                                 IS `replaced`
        `damaged by the same cause at the same time as other parts in the same accident` IS TRUE
        `stolen`                                                   IS FALSE
        `damaged by overload, overpressure, short circuit, self-heating, arcing or leakage` IS FALSE
        `years the traction battery has been used`                 IS 0
        `sum insured listed for this added equipment`              IS NOTHING

-- A tyre burst on its own, not with other parts (Article 13.7).
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`a tyre damaged alone` MEANS
    `A damaged item` WITH
        `kind`                                                     IS `a tyre or inner tube`
        `cost`                                                     IS 4000000
        `replaced`                                                 IS TRUE
        `damaged by the same cause at the same time as other parts in the same accident` IS FALSE
        `stolen`                                                   IS FALSE
        `damaged by overload, overpressure, short circuit, self-heating, arcing or leakage` IS FALSE
        `years the traction battery has been used`                 IS 0
        `sum insured listed for this added equipment`              IS NOTHING

-- A stolen wing mirror (Article 13.3, BS04).
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`a stolen mirror` MEANS
    `A damaged item` WITH
        `kind`                                                     IS `an ordinary part`
        `cost`                                                     IS 15000000
        `replaced`                                                 IS TRUE
        `damaged by the same cause at the same time as other parts in the same accident` IS FALSE
        `stolen`                                                   IS TRUE
        `damaged by overload, overpressure, short circuit, self-heating, arcing or leakage` IS FALSE
        `years the traction battery has been used`                 IS 0
        `sum insured listed for this added equipment`              IS NOTHING

-- A replaced traction battery of a given age, in years.
GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`a traction battery aged` `the age` MEANS
    `A damaged item` WITH
        `kind`                                                     IS `the traction battery`
        `cost`                                                     IS 200000000
        `replaced`                                                 IS TRUE
        `damaged by the same cause at the same time as other parts in the same accident` IS TRUE
        `stolen`                                                   IS FALSE
        `damaged by overload, overpressure, short circuit, self-heating, arcing or leakage` IS FALSE
        `years the traction battery has been used`                 IS `the age`
        `sum insured listed for this added equipment`              IS NOTHING

-- The collision scenario: bumper replaced (20 million), headlamp repaired (10 million), tyre
-- replaced with the other parts (4 million), windscreen replaced (6 million); towing 2 million.
GIVETH A LIST OF `A damaged item`
`the collision damage` MEANS
    LIST `an item` `an ordinary part` `costing` 20000000 `, replaced:` TRUE,
         `an item` `an electrical or electronic part, or an engine` `costing` 10000000 `, replaced:` FALSE,
         `an item` `a tyre or inner tube` `costing` 4000000 `, replaced:` TRUE,
         `an item` `windscreen or mirror glass` `costing` 6000000 `, replaced:` TRUE

GIVEN `the cause`          IS A `A cause of own damage`
      `the items`          IS A LIST OF `A damaged item`
      `estimate`           IS A NUMBER
      `value before`       IS A NUMBER
      `decision`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `flooded`            IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An own-damage loss`
`a loss by` `the cause` `of` `the items` `, estimate` `estimate` `, value before` `value before` `, theft decided:` `decision` `, flooded:` `flooded` MEANS
    `An own-damage loss` WITH
        `cause`                                                          IS `the cause`
        `sudden and unforeseen`                                          IS TRUE
        `items`                                                          IS `the items`
        `cost of preventing further loss`                                IS 0
        `cost of rescue and towing to the nearest repairer`              IS 2000000
        `market value immediately before the loss`                       IS `value before`
        `estimated cost of repair`                                       IS `estimate`
        `investigation concluded or suspended, or prosecution declined`  IS `decision`
        `more than half the paint area damaged`                          IS FALSE
        `cost of repainting the whole vehicle`                           IS 0
        `whole vehicle lost by fraud, breach of trust, civil dispute or unknown cause` IS FALSE
        `wear and tear, inherent vice, loss of value, defect or faulty repair`        IS FALSE
        `vehicle operating in a flooded area`                            IS `flooded`
        `caused by the traction battery`                                 IS FALSE
        `caused by incompatible equipment`                               IS FALSE
        `caused by handling outside the manufacturer's standards`        IS FALSE
        `caused by equipment added after manufacture`                    IS FALSE
        `during operation of special equipment`                          IS FALSE
        `caused by a bomb, mine or explosive device`                     IS FALSE
        `repaired in Vietnam`                                            IS TRUE
        `the owner keeps the vehicle`                                    IS FALSE
        `sums insured by other contracts on the same vehicle`            IS 0

GIVETH AN `An own-damage loss`
`the collision` MEANS
    `a loss by` `collision, overturning, falling, sinking or impact by an external object` `of` `the collision damage`
        `, estimate` 40000000 `, value before` 780000000 `, theft decided:` FALSE `, flooded:` FALSE

§§ `Facts for the additional clauses`

GIVEN `thefts already claimed` IS A NUMBER
      `days of repair`         IS A NUMBER
      `hire per day`           IS A NUMBER
      `hire days already paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Facts for the additional clauses`
`clause facts with` `thefts already claimed` `thefts claimed,` `days of repair` `days of repair at` `hire per day` `a day,` `hire days already paid` `days already paid` MEANS
    `Facts for the additional clauses` WITH
        `part thefts already claimed under this contract`                               IS `thefts already claimed`
        `licensed to circulate in that country`                                         IS TRUE
        `driver licensed in that country`                                               IS TRUE
        `temporarily imported for re-export, duty-free, or a diplomatic vehicle`        IS FALSE
        `days of repair, from the repair contract to the acceptance record`             IS `days of repair`
        `hire cost per day, before VAT`                                                 IS `hire per day`
        `days of hire already paid in the period`                                       IS `hire days already paid`
        `new with a factory quality slip, or imported with a quality certificate and customs papers` IS FALSE
        `used only inside a closed site, never on public roads, with chassis and engine numbers`     IS FALSE
        `loss inside the closed site`                                                   IS FALSE
        `a qualifying driving-school vehicle driven by a learner in traffic`            IS FALSE
        `learner not listed, or without card, learner's permit or papers`               IS FALSE
        `instructor without a practising certificate`                                   IS FALSE
        `no learner sign or no auxiliary brake`                                         IS FALSE
        `outside the school's permitted time or route`                                  IS FALSE
        `no instructor beside the learner, outside a test`                              IS FALSE
        `special vehicle not technically safe`                                          IS FALSE
        `operator without the right licence for the special equipment`                  IS FALSE
        `operator deliberately broke the operating instructions`                        IS FALSE
        `a converted or modified goods vehicle`                                         IS FALSE
        `inspection certificate expired at the loss`                                    IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Facts for the additional clauses`
`no clause facts` MEANS `clause facts with` 0 `thefts claimed,` 0 `days of repair at` 0 `a day,` 0 `days already paid`
